d"},{"n":"Fort Sherman","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":9.36302,"lo":-79.953035,"d":5835,"ds":"Fort Sherman is a former United States Army base in Panama, located on Toro Point at the Caribbean (northern) end of the Panama Canal, on the western bank of the Canal directly opposite Colón (which is on the eastern bank). It was the primary defensive base for the Caribbean sector of the Canal from 1914–1945, and was also the U.S. Army Caribbean's Jungle Warfare Training Center (JWTC) from 1951–1999.","wpu":"Fort Sherman","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d4/Ft_sherman_panama.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Fort Gulick","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":9.316667,"lo":-79.866667,"d":5961,"ds":"Fort Gulick was a United States Army base in the former Panama Canal Zone located on the Atlantic side of the Panama Canal near Fort Davis, on Gatun Lake.","wpu":"Fort Gulick","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Panam%C3%A1_-_Escuela_de_las_Americas_-_2006.JPG/960px-Panam%C3%A1_-_Escuela_de_las_Americas_-_2006.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Atlantic Bridge, Panama","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":9.3081,"lo":-79.9189,"d":6027,"ds":"The Atlantic Bridge (Spanish: Puente Atlántico) is a road bridge in Colón, Panama spanning the Atlantic entrance to the Panama Canal. Completed in 2019, it is the third bridge over the canal after the Bridge of the Americas and the Centennial Bridge, both on the Pacific side of the canal.","wpu":"Atlantic Bridge, Panama","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Puente_del_Atl%C3%A1ntico_del_Canal_de_Panam%C3%A1_.jpg/960px-Puente_del_Atl%C3%A1ntico_del_Canal_de_Panam%C3%A1_.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Colón (Spanish pronunciation: [koˈlon]) is a city and seaport in Panama, beside the Caribbean Sea, lying near the Atlantic entrance to the Panama Canal. It is the capital of Panama's Colón Province and has traditionally been known as Panama's second city. City proper located entirely on Manzanillo Peninsula (former island), surrounded by Limon Bay, Manzanillo Bay, and the Folks River.","wpu":"Colón, Panama","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/CO-colon-2000-02.jpg/960px-CO-colon-2000-02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}